The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (cdclk > 312000)
```
Reason:
This condition does not account for the new cdclk values of 324/326.4, which means that when cdclk exceeds 312000 but is less than or equal to 326400, the voltage level may be incorrectly assigned, leading to potential hardware issues.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (cdclk > 326400)
	return 3;
else if (cdclk > 312000)
	return 2;
```
Reason:
These updated conditions correctly reflect the new voltage level requirements based on the latest bspec, ensuring that cdclk values above 326400 are assigned the correct voltage level of 3, while values between 312000 and 326400 are assigned the correct voltage level of 2.

